response.rawText:
{"text":"Yes. Tens PADS can often be placed near or around the area of pain to help target discomfort. However, avoid placing pads directly over the areas where they are not recommended, such as the front of the neck, head, open wounds, irritated skin, or directly over bony areas. For the best results, try placing the pads around the painful area rather than directly on the most sensitive spot.

Useful Resources & Links:
📋 [TENS Electrode Placement Chart](https://paintechnology.s3.amazonaws.com/pdf/placementchart.pdf)"}

